Subject: [PATCH] prov/verbs: register CUDA memory via dma-buf, and close the fd

Two fixes needed on a dmabuf-only platform (NVIDIA open kernel module, no
peermem -- DOCA 3.4 does not export ib_register_peer_memory_client):

1. vrb_mr_reg_common() routed only ZE/SYNAPSEAI/ROCR through the dma-buf
   registration helper and fell back to ibv_reg_mr() for CUDA, which fails
   with EFAULT (-14) when there is no peer-memory client. Add FI_HMEM_CUDA.
   (Upstream main already does this via `iface != FI_HMEM_SYSTEM`; this
   hunk is only needed for the 1.25 tree DAOS bundles.)

2. vrb_reg_hmem_dmabuf() never closed the dma-buf fd obtained from
   ofi_hmem_get_dmabuf_fd(). The MR holds its own reference, so the fd is
   only needed for the call; leaving it open leaks one fd per registration.
   With the MR cache disabled (Mercury forces FI_MR_CACHE_MAX_COUNT=0),
   reading 8 GiB in 4 MiB chunks exhausts nofile=1024 and
   cuMemGetHandleForAddressRange() then fails with
   CUDA_ERROR_OPERATING_SYSTEM. Measured: 634 open dma-buf fds after 1.5 s
   of I/O; 1 after this change.

Applies to the libfabric 1.25 tree that DAOS builds as a prerequisite.
See gpudirect/README.md, section "GDS over ofi+verbs".
---
diff --git a/prov/verbs/src/verbs_mr.c b/prov/verbs/src/verbs_mr.c
index eb86c0272..f8bacfd41 100644
--- a/prov/verbs/src/verbs_mr.c
+++ b/prov/verbs/src/verbs_mr.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <ofi_util.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 #include "verbs_ofi.h"
 
 static int vrb_mr_close(fid_t fid)
@@ -86,6 +87,13 @@ static struct ibv_mr *vrb_reg_hmem_dmabuf(enum fi_hmem_iface iface,
 
 	mr = ibv_reg_dmabuf_mr(pd, offset, len, (uint64_t)buf/* iova */,
 			       fd, vrb_access);
+	saved_errno = errno;
+	/* The MR holds its own reference to the dma-buf; without this close
+	 * every registration leaks one fd and long runs die on EMFILE
+	 * (cuMemGetHandleForAddressRange -> CUDA_ERROR_OPERATING_SYSTEM). */
+	close(fd);
+	errno = saved_errno;
+	saved_errno = 0;
 	if (!mr && failover_policy[iface] == TRY &&
 	    vrb_gl_data.peer_mem_support) {
 		saved_errno = errno;
@@ -145,7 +153,8 @@ vrb_mr_reg_common(struct vrb_mem_desc *md, int vrb_access, const void *base_addr
 	else if (vrb_gl_data.dmabuf_support &&
 		 (iface == FI_HMEM_ZE ||
 		  iface == FI_HMEM_SYNAPSEAI ||
-		  iface == FI_HMEM_ROCR))
+		  iface == FI_HMEM_ROCR ||
+		  iface == FI_HMEM_CUDA))  /* dmabuf-only platforms (no peermem) */
 		md->mr = vrb_reg_hmem_dmabuf(iface, md->domain->pd, buf, len,
 						vrb_access);
 	else
